      "message": "This appears to be the only time we take action on `fInitialized` and we assert that its state matches `fVar`. We used to use `fVar` directly, but presumably we can\u0027t use it directly anymore--why not? Because of poison?\n\n(If so, can we just check for \"var is null or var is Poison/var type is Invalid\" instead of having a new member?)",
